Subject: udev backend: let emulators opt in to a software EGL renderer

QEMU's virtio-gpu without host GL (e.g. on macOS) only offers llvmpipe, which the
compositor skips. MECHANIX_ALLOW_SOFTWARE_EGL=1 accepts it.

Upstream: mecha-org/mechanix-comp, against main c0d551b (packaged 1.0.0-2).

diff --git a/src/backend/udev.rs b/src/backend/udev.rs
index b25e5ab..a313652 100644
--- a/src/backend/udev.rs
+++ b/src/backend/udev.rs
@@ -521,9 +521,11 @@ impl State<UdevData> {
                 }
             };
             let egl_device = EGLDevice::device_for_display(&egl_display).ok();
+            // Emulators without host GL (e.g. QEMU virtio-gpu on macOS) only have llvmpipe; let them opt in.
             if egl_device
                 .as_ref()
                 .is_some_and(|device| device.is_software())
+                && std::env::var_os("MECHANIX_ALLOW_SOFTWARE_EGL").is_none()
             {
                 warn!("Ignoring {node}: software EGL renderer");
                 return Ok(());
